diff --git a/sdk/protocol/README.md b/sdk/protocol/README.md
index 3bb637f..409bd5c 100644
--- a/sdk/protocol/README.md
+++ b/sdk/protocol/README.md
@@ -1,24 +1,30 @@
-# Standalone CPA protocol contracts
+# Standalone CPA Codex accounting and wire codec
 
 Module: `github.com/router-for-me/CLIProxyAPI/sdk/protocol`.
-The canonical location is `sdk/protocol` in the patched CPA source. This module
-uses only the Go standard library. Importing it does not load the host, plugin
-runtime, translator, scheduler, or infra cache.
+The canonical source is `sdk/protocol` in the patched CPA checkout. This module
+uses the Go standard library and its own decoded accounting package.
 
-`codex` describes Responses/Lite usage attribution, tool catalogs and completed
-call/result history, metadata and turn-state transport. `Response` and `Event`
-are inspection views. Retain the original wire when forwarding opaque or unknown
-fields. The echoed tool catalog does not prove that tools can execute.
+`codex` owns decoded cache counters, recursive row constraints and complete
+attribution partitions. Its validation reads caller evidence without changing it.
+It does not decode JSON or change transport metadata.
 
-`Usage.Validate()` checks reported counters and complete attribution partitions.
-Check `InputKnown` separately when explicit accounting is required. Unknown reads
-and writes remain unknown. Aggregate input minus reads is not a cache-write count.
-`Usage.EvidenceErr` and `MetadataHeaders.Err` are deferred decoding errors: this
-lets callers give an upstream failure priority over missing accounting evidence.
-Callers must check them before using the evidence.
+`codexwire` owns Responses/Lite JSON inspection, envelope decoding, tool catalogs,
+call/result history, metadata parsing and metadata rewrites. Import `Response`,
+`Event`, `Usage` and the wire operations from this package. Their mutable JSON
+decoder methods and metadata setters remain with this complete codec operation.
+No aliases remain at the former wire API location.
 
-The protocol types do not establish model identity, classify BPS, select routes,
-or authorize release. Those decisions belong to the consumer. The shared JSON
-vectors under `codex/testdata` test the same accounting cases in Go and Rust.
+`Response` and `Event` are inspection views. Forward the original bytes to retain
+unknown fields and opaque output. Duplicate markers belong to one envelope;
+reusing a decode destination replaces its earlier evidence. `Usage.EvidenceErr`
+and `MetadataHeaders.Err` retain deferred errors. Check them before using evidence
+so an upstream failure can keep priority over incomplete accounting.
 
-Run `GOWORK=off go test -race ./...` from this directory.
+`Usage.Validate()` checks reported counts and complete attribution partitions.
+Check `InputKnown` separately when explicit input accounting is required. Unknown
+reads and writes remain unknown. Input minus reads is not a cache-write count.
+The echoed tool catalog does not establish that a tool can execute.
+
+Run `GOWORK=off go test -race ./...` from this directory. The wire codec tests use
+the shared usage vectors under `codexwire/testdata` and exercise real JSON decoding,
+reused envelopes, duplicate evidence, metadata rewrites and tool history.
